@startuml SCRUM-66 Platform auction rules schema

title Platform auction rules — schema design (SCRUM-66)\nSource of truth: FYP/src/main/resources/db/migration_platform_rules.sql

skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam linetype ortho
hide circle

' ============================================================
' Configuration table (single row)
' ============================================================
entity "platform_rules" as platform_rules {
  * id : SMALLINT <<PK>> = 1
  --
  * min_bid_increment : NUMERIC(10,2) = 1.00
  * max_auction_duration_days : INT = 30
  * updated_at : TIMESTAMPTZ = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
  updated_by : BIGINT <<FK→users>>
  ..constraints..
  CHECK (id = 1) — singleton row
  CHECK (min_bid_increment BETWEEN 0.01 AND 10000.00)
  CHECK (max_auction_duration_days BETWEEN 1 AND 365)
}

entity "users" as users {
  * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
  --
  * role_id : SMALLINT <<FK→roles>>
  ..note..
  only ADMIN may write the rules
}

' ============================================================
' Tables validated against the rules (existing schema, abridged)
' ============================================================
entity "auction" as auction {
  * auction_id : BIGINT <<PK>>
  --
  * date_created : TIMESTAMPTZ
  * date_end : TIMESTAMPTZ
  * status_id : SMALLINT
  * seller_id : BIGINT
  ..rule..
  date_end - date_created <= max_auction_duration_days
}

entity "bids" as bids {
  * bid_id : BIGINT <<PK>>
  --
  * auction_id : BIGINT <<FK→auction>>
  * user_id : BIGINT <<FK→users>>
  * bid_amount : NUMERIC(10,2)
  * bid_time : TIMESTAMPTZ
  ..rule..
  bid_amount >= current price + min_bid_increment
}

entity "auto_bids" as auto_bids {
  * id : BIGINT <<PK>>
  --
  * auction_id : BIGINT <<FK→auction>>
  * user_id : BIGINT <<FK→users>>
  * max_amount_enc : TEXT
  * bid_increment : NUMERIC(10,2)
  ..rule..
  per-buyer step clamped up to min_bid_increment
}

platform_rules }o--|| users : updated_by

' ============================================================
' Design notes
' ============================================================
note as WHY_SINGLETON
  **Why a single-row table and not a key/value store**
  Both rules are typed (money / whole days) and are read on
  every bid and every listing creation. A typed single row
  gives DB-level CHECK constraints, one cheap SELECT, and no
  string parsing. `CHECK (id = 1)` makes a second row
  impossible, so the table can never disagree with itself.
end note

note as WHY_NO_FK_CASCADE
  **updated_by is nullable, no ON DELETE**
  The seeded defaults have no author. If an admin account is
  ever removed the rules must survive, so the FK is a plain
  reference with no cascade.
end note

note as ENFORCEMENT
  **Enforcement points (SCRUM-67)**
  min_bid_increment
    · BidDAO.placeBid — manual bid must reach
      max(starting_price, highest bid) + min_bid_increment
    · AutoBidDAO — proxy steps clamped up to the rule
  max_auction_duration_days
    · SellerApiServlet create/edit (POST /api/seller/create, /edit)
    · CreateAuctionServlet (legacy /create-auction)

  Not enforced (by design): Dutch auctions have no bid steps
  (price descends on a clock) and blind auctions are sealed,
  so there is no visible current price to increment over.
end note

note as MIGRATION
  **Rollout**
  migration_platform_rules.sql is idempotent and seeds row 1.
  If the table is missing (older DB), PlatformRulesDAO falls
  back to the same defaults ($1.00 / 30 days) so bidding and
  listing keep working.
end note

platform_rules .. WHY_SINGLETON
platform_rules .. WHY_NO_FK_CASCADE
bids .. ENFORCEMENT
auction .. MIGRATION

@enduml
